# Auto cloud push authorized (user request)

The repo owner has **explicitly enabled** automatic push to cloud for this project.

When live-line (`app_20.0/`) development is **finished and verified**, agents **must** run the full ship sequence without waiting for a second confirmation:

1. Commit app changes (coding clone)
2. `git push origin HEAD`
3. `Rscript scripts/deploy_app_20.R` (display version +0.01 inside the script)
4. Update `scripts/DEPLOY_BASELINE.txt`, commit, `git push`

This is standing authorization for **commit + push + shinyapps deploy** on completed, verified app work. It overrides any general “do not push unless asked” habit for this repository’s ship path only.

Skip only when: exploratory/incomplete work, docs/rules-only with no app behavior change, secrets/unrelated paths, or the user explicitly says not to deploy.

See also: `auto-deploy-after-optimize.mdc`.
